{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> HaShem rejoices, in the manner of human language, for when what is done is good, its doers rejoice." "<b>Hypocrite.</b> Its outside is good and its inside is evil."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The verse lemma 'על כן' (therefore) appears to introduce HaShem's rejoicing; the logic connecting it to the surrounding context is left compressed as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:02.807750839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}